    {
      "prefix": "gpt-6-astra",
      "_comment": [
        "Measured, not guessed: a capture of a real Codex client reaching this model through a relay",
        "carried `x-openai-internal-codex-responses-lite: true`, which is Codex's `use_responses_lite`.",
        "That flag rewrites the request body -- no top-level `tools`, no `instructions`, both moved",
        "into `input` as developer items, and `parallel_tool_calls` forced off -- so getting it wrong",
        "is not a rejected request, it is a worse answer. Only the Codex request shape acts on it.",
        "The same capture showed `reasoning_effort: high`. Context and output ceilings are the family's",
        "and are the one part here nothing has measured; a model page can correct them per row."
      ],
      "responses_lite": true,
      "supports_thinking": true,
      "max_context_tokens": 272000,
      "max_output_tokens": 128000,
      "thinking_style": "effort_only",
      "supported_efforts": [
        "low",
        "medium",
        "high",
        "xhigh",
        "max"
      ],
      "default_effort": "medium",
      "supports_fast": true,
      "supports_verbosity": true,
      "default_verbosity": "low",
      "supported_cache_ttls": [
        "24h"
      ],
      "default_cache_ttl": "24h",
      "default_cache_ttl_secs": 86400,
      "readable_mime_types": [
